{"skill":{"slug":"bilibili-hot-monitor","displayName":"B站 (bilibili) 热门视频监控"},"version":{"version":"1.0.21","createdAt":1770536492731,"changelog":"修复进度条","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":".gitignore","size":376,"sha256":"b226754a480ba5c3f8024c9aeb5a62886a9f57de79973cab9909fc14b99f6d48","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"bilibili-monitor.example.json","size":192,"sha256":"59a3593f35a3110041d1727778152cb435e5a00c4792396345a40cdaba15a05d","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"bilibili_api.py","size":12370,"sha256":"c50106186ec94f6fe604f3200a12ef8761f6c6c083501016513b4bf57a874f83","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"bilibili_subtitle.py","size":7424,"sha256":"22e6f30eefde82d66b143d479f596ac0f2acdcbec7abff6f29a8468213bac06b","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"example_report.md","size":19246,"sha256":"dd227d9a6849340e45c6ea9dc4a1b0ab79470be63c7f3e000668f3ed704d514a","contentType":null},{"path":"generate_report.py","size":28749,"sha256":"f5975ee57eb3c31534383c616c37dd946b334f44dd144f01ca8b27223acce1cb","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"README.md","size":5506,"sha256":"394bd942441cf2b6370a985f9c2b1ba4ae55d8f25adcc10892591a7472e318fe","contentType":null},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":18,"sha256":"c8420eac351a9df0a25beab7f0fc067bfb4e672a3c51cf8796fe2727e762e58e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"send_email.py","size":13285,"sha256":"d605ddf86d243980dc0824d7fcfa94874052662ed4401f8f89635d955e013d02","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4895,"sha256":"ca27d733e0ccdd75a9a2294527e806d8c3b82626c82187b742aee4935f1857de","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2587,"sha256":"4d1064a3da33fe3234efab52812986c6379267cade51e4df0adffb2439d85e89","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789029350456,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"6cd0fd95137057945d97686b3191f953d687a75d73fc41e112b805a682b17e03","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/6cd0fd95137057945d97686b3191f953d687a75d73fc41e112b805a682b17e03","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: bilibili-hot-monitor\nVersion: 1.0.21\n\nThe skill bundle is designed to generate Bilibili hot video reports and send them via email, optionally using AI for summaries and comments. It handles sensitive credentials (Bilibili cookies, OpenRouter API key, SMTP credentials) by instructing the user to provide them via environment variables, command-line arguments, or a local configuration file, which is a secure practice. All network connections are to legitimate Bilibili APIs, OpenRouter AI (openrouter.ai), and a user-configured SMTP server (defaulting to smtp.gmail.com), aligning with its stated purpose. While SKILL.md contains instructions for the AI agent to control its output during execution (e.g., '请只转发脚本实际输出' - 'please only forward the script's actual output'), these are framed as improving user experience and preventing chat spam, not for hiding malicious activities. There is no evidence of data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or other intentional harmful behaviors.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160937356},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":38,"checkedAt":1789029350456},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill appears purpose-aligned, but it needs review because it asks for and stores reusable Bilibili cookies, an OpenRouter key, and SMTP credentials in plaintext while sending video subtitle content to external services.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access to Bilibili, OpenRouter, and SMTP is coherent with the feature set, but subtitle/title/metadata content is sent to OpenRouter and email recipients, and the disclosure does not clearly explain third-party handling or retention implications.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package uses local Python files and a single common dependency, requests; I found no install-time remote payload execution, tool wrapping, startup hook, or scheduled persistence mechanism.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill uses broad trigger phrases such as '热门视频' and '视频日报' and then may prompt for credentials and perform networked report generation plus email sending; it does include a confirmation before execution, but activation scope is still broad.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The SKILL.md first-use flow writes Bilibili cookies, an OpenRouter API key, SMTP email, and SMTP app password into bilibili-monitor.json in plaintext without owner-only permissions; the scripts also support passing secrets through command-line arguments.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Generating Bilibili hot-video reports, summarizing subtitles with OpenRouter, and sending email match the stated purpose; the required Bilibili session cookies, OpenRouter key, and SMTP credentials are high-impact but related to those features.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving the skill Bilibili session cookies, optional OpenRouter API access, and SMTP sending authority. Prefer environment variables or a secret manager over the generated plaintext config, avoid command-line secrets, use an app-specific email password, review recipients before sending, and assume subtitles/titles/metadata may be shared with OpenRouter and email recipients.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The .gitignore references to .env and bilibili-monitor.json are protective ignore rules rather than evidence of credential-file harvesting, so this finding is downgraded.\n[TP4] expected: OpenRouter processing and SMTP sending are disclosed and purpose-aligned, but the combination of external subtitle processing and local multi-secret storage is a real review concern.\n[SDI-1] expected: Subtitle retrieval and video-detail helpers support the advertised report workflow; the standalone arbitrary-video subtitle script broadens the package but is not invoked by the main skill flow.\n[P2] expected: The detected hidden character in example_report.md appears inside copied Bilibili author text, not as an instruction to the agent.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending subtitle-derived prompts to OpenRouter is expected for LLM summaries and is mentioned in the README/SKILL, but users should receive clearer disclosure before content leaves the local environment.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The trigger phrases are generic enough to cause unintended activation for ordinary Bilibili or hot-video requests, though the skill does ask before executing the full workflow.\n[LP3] expected: File writes, network access, and credential use are necessary for the workflow, but explicit boundaries and safer secret handling are missing.\n[E1] expected: Outbound requests to Bilibili and OpenRouter are core to the report and AI-summary features; they are security-relevant but not exfiltration by themselves.\n[SDI-2] expected: Using SESSDATA or full cookies is related to authenticated Bilibili subtitle access, but raw reusable session credentials materially raise account-risk if mishandled.\n[SQP-3] expected: Defaulting to Chinese subtitles is consistent with a Chinese Bilibili daily-report skill and is not a security concern.\n[T09] unexpected: Plaintext storage of Bilibili cookies, OpenRouter keys, and SMTP passwords in bilibili-monitor.json is a validated concern because no restrictive permissions or secure storage are applied.\n[T09] unexpected: Command-line options for cookies, OpenRouter keys, and SMTP passwords can expose secrets through shell history, process listings, or logs.\n[T09] unexpected: The HTML email converter interpolates unescaped Bilibili/report/model content into HTML, allowing injected markup in outgoing reports.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789029350456}}}}}